Aurora on the emulator product, and nowhere else.

ADR-013: this patch carries the observer, not the subject. Deleting it leaves every Aurora
artifact unchanged and leaves lineage_beyond2lte carrying Aurora through a device tree Aurora
owns; what disappears is the ability to watch it start. The day a beyond2lte device exists, this
file is deleted and no Aurora source changes.

Three settings, and all of them only say that Aurora exists on this product:

  PRODUCT_PACKAGES            installs the jar. Added after the first build failed, and the
                              failure is worth keeping: declaring a system server jar without
                              installing it produces no dexpreopt artifacts, and AOSP's
                              dex_preopt_check refuses the build rather than shipping a classpath
                              entry with nothing behind it.

                                Offending entries:
                                  system/framework/oat/x86_64/aurora-platform-android.odex
                                  system/framework/oat/x86_64/aurora-platform-android.vdex

                              Classpath membership and installation are separate facts, and only
                              a real build says so.

  PRODUCT_SYSTEM_SERVER_JARS_EXTRA
                              puts aurora-platform-android on the system server's classloader,
                              which is where SystemServer resolves a device-specific service by
                              name. The _EXTRA variant, and the system_ext: prefix, because the
                              second build failed on this:

                                internal error: Device makefile produces files inside
                                build/make/target/product/generic_system.mk's artifact path
                                requirement.

                              Installing into system/framework put Aurora inside a requirement
                              that exists to keep the generic system image identical everywhere.
                              Aurora is by definition not part of that image, system_ext is the
                              partition for what a product adds, and device/google/atv already
                              reaches the classpath the same way for tv-services. The alternative
                              was an entry in PRODUCT_ARTIFACT_PATH_REQUIREMENT_ALLOWED_LIST -
                              an exemption from a rule Aurora has no argument with.

  PRODUCT_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS    points at frameworks/base/aurora/overlay, which is Aurora's. The
                              array naming AuroraSystemService lives there rather than here, so
                              this patch holds no Aurora decisions.

diff --git a/build/target/product/lineage_sdk_phone_x86_64.mk b/build/target/product/lineage_sdk_phone_x86_64.mk
--- a/build/target/product/lineage_sdk_phone_x86_64.mk
+++ b/build/target/product/lineage_sdk_phone_x86_64.mk
@@ -38,4 +38,16 @@
 PRODUCT_SDK_ADDON_COPY_FILES += \
     device/generic/goldfish/data/etc/advancedFeatures.ini:images/x86_64/advancedFeatures.ini \
     device/generic/goldfish/data/etc/encryptionkey.img:images/x86_64/encryptionkey.img \
     $(EMULATOR_KERNEL_FILE):images/x86_64/kernel-ranchu
+
+# Aurora, on this product only. See ADR-013 in the Aurora tree: the emulator is the only
+# product this checkout can boot, and its makefile is upstream, so observing Aurora start
+# requires a patch that observing it on a real device would not.
+PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+    aurora-platform-android
+
+PRODUCT_SYSTEM_SERVER_JARS_EXTRA += \
+    system_ext:aurora-platform-android
+
+PRODUCT_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS += \
+    frameworks/base/aurora/overlay
